 "capsule": "The Joseon dynasty (조선), founded in 1392 when General Yi Seong-gye (Taejo) deposed the last Goryeo king and moved the capital to Hanseong (modern Seoul), ruled the Korean peninsula for over five centuries under a Confucian bureaucratic state modeled on Ming China. Its long span encompassed the creation of the Hangul script under King Sejong, the devastating Imjin War with Japan (1592–1598), and late Enlightenment-era reforms, before ending formally when King Gojong proclaimed the Korean Empire in 1897. This dynasty is unrelated to the far older Gojoseon/Wiman Joseon kingdom of the 2nd century BCE that happens to share this entry's Wikidata identifier.",
